{#
/**
 * @file
 * Template for the frontpage.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - site_url: the base url of our page.
 */
#}
{% extends 'base/base.twig' %}

{% block content %}
  <h1 class="mt-5">ESN Simple Web Developing test</h1>

  <div class="tasks_container">
    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 1 <span class="badge badge-easy">Easy</span></div>
      <div class="task">If you see this page, then you have succeeded the first task. You can proceed now with the next tasks but before continuing, please take a look to what is included in this page and to the following advices:</div>

      <div class="hints alert alert-primary" role="alert">
        The following libraries are already installed and ready-to-use. Information about them can be found in their respective websites:
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://getbootstrap.com/" target="_blank" title="bootstrap page">Bootstrap</a> (version 5.1.3),</li>
          <li><a href="https://twig.symfony.com/" target="_blank" title="twig page">Twig</a> (version 3.30.0) with debug enabled and dump() function available,</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/lipis/flag-icon-css" target="_blank" title="flag-icon-css github page">Flag-icon-css</a> (version 7.6.0),</li>
          <li><a href="https://fontawesome.com/" target="_blank" title="fontwawesome page">FontAwesome</a> (version 5.11.2),</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/PHPOffice/PhpSpreadsheet/" target="_blank" title="Php Spreadsheet github page">PhpOffice/phpspreadsheet</a> (version 1.30.8).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hints alert alert-success" role="alert">
        <ul>
          <li>Read the description of each task carefully, as might contain some clues or guidance for finishing the task.</li>
          <li>Following coding standards (PHP or even Drupal ones) will be highly valued, as well readability and cleaninness of the code and number of lines used.</li>
          <li>The result of each task will be displayed right after the task description and before the next one. Cache is disabled, so the output should appear automatically each time the page is refreshed.</li>
          <li>In order to finish the task, the <strong>main</strong> goal is required. Finishing the optional subtasks are not mandatory but recommended.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hints alert alert-warning" role="alert">Each task tells you which file needs to be edited or created. Any other existing file must not be edited, but in some tasks it is mentioned to take a look to some files as might be interesting for finalizing the task successfully.</div>
    </div>

    <hr class="separation">

    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 2 <span class="badge badge-easy">Easy</span></div>
      <div class="task">Your first task is to finish the code inside the block <code>solution_news</code> located in the file <code>templates/test/blocks_test.twig</code>, as right now it is empty.</div>
      <div class="task">All the data needed for this task is already available in the twig file (as is mentioned in the header); you just need to render as required by the task.</div>
      <div class="task"><strong>The main requirements are:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Using the bootstrap <strong>Card component</strong>, render a preview of the last three articles available form the list.</li>
          <li>The three articles need to appear horizontally, one next to the other, and with the proper separation in between each article.</li>
          <li>The preview must contain the title, the date, the first 200 chars of the article followed by '...' (or just the full article if the length is less), and a 'Read more' link (use '#' for now).</li>
          <li>If extra css is needed, you have the <code>assets/css/test_style.css</code> file available.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="task"><em>The optional requirements are:</em>
        <ul>
          <li>The preview render as well the image available (if any) or a placeholder from <a href="https://placehold.co/" target="_blank">https://placehold.co/</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      {% set text_hint = (num_articles == 0
        ? 'It seems there is an error and no articles have been fetched. Please override the getNews() function in your TestController.php file and load the local file in assets/json.'
        : 'There are ' ~ num_articles ~ ' articles fetched and you can proceed with the task.'
      ) %}
      <div class="hints alert alert-primary" role="alert">
        <div><strong>Some hints:</strong></div>
        <div>{{ text_hint }}</div>
      </div>

      <div class="solution_container">
        {% block solution_news %}
          <div class="solution_header">The solution for task 2 will appear here after the block is finished.</div>
        {% endblock %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="separation">

    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 3 <span class="badge badge-medium">Medium</span></div>
      <div class="task">In task 2 you created a block that renders the last 3 articles, but there is no <code>/articles</code> page where you can render the full list. Could be interesting to have one.</div>
      <div class="task"><strong>The main requirements are:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Create a first route (eg: <code>articles</code>) to render the list of all articles fetched and available. This design is up to you.</li>
          <li>Create a second route (up to you) to render the each individual article in full based on the article ID. The design is up to you.</li>
          <li>Update the <code>src/Test/TestView.php</code> class to add any new route(s)/method(s) that you need for the requirements.</li>
          <li>Use the <code>src/Test/TestController.php</code> class to add any new methods you need.</li>
          <li>Place your templates in the folder <code>templates/test</code> and for the CSS you can use the <code>assets/css/test_style.css</code> file.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="task"><em>The optional requirements are:</em>
        <ul>
          <li>Create a last route (up to you) to render the each individual article in full based on the article slug. The code is up to you.</li>
          <li>Redirect the user to the 404 page if the ID/slug does not find a match.</li>
          <li>Alter the code of task 2 to include the new routes created for proper navigation at your discretion.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hints alert alert-primary" role="alert">
        <div><strong>Some hints:</strong></div>
        <div>
          <ul>
            <li>For your templates, you can extend the <code>base/base.twig</code> template like the <code>front/front.twig</code> does, so you just need to override the content block and use your own variables.</li>
            <li>You can define a route with variables such as <code>'my-route/{param}'</code> but you cannot have two different methods using the same route (excluding the variable).</li>
            <li>Views (and routes) are loaded automatically once they are created. You can use the <code>front()</code> function in the <code>TestView.php</code> as example. Any variable needed by the route can be used in the method directly.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hints alert alert-warning" role="alert">
        <div>
          There should be no issues with caches and DDEV but if you experience some, check how to add a custom DDEV <code>php.ini</code> to disable OPCACHE or similar.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="solution_container">
        <div class="solution_header">Solution to task 3</div>
        <div>Link <a href="{{ site_url }}/articles" title="Articles page">Articles</a> should be working after the solution is done; as well as further navigation.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="separation">

    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 4 <span class="badge badge-advanced">Advanced</span></div>
      <div class="task">As you might have noticed while working on <code>src/Test/TestController.php</code> in the previous task, there are also a few methods that are incompleted and now it is time to finish them; however there are other functions in the class inherited that can be used for this task.</div>
      <div class="task">We want to render all the data of countries and sections of ESN International using a bootstrap accordion. This accordion must contain <en>each ESN country per group item (header)</en> and <em>all of the sections belonging to this country in the accordion panel</em>. In the header it must appear the flag and name of the country and the number of the sections belonging to it. The list of ESN sections that belongs to that country needs to be placed inside the panel. All the panes must be collapsible and must stay closed the moment the accordion is firstly rendered.</div>
      <div class="task"><strong>The main requirements are:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Complete the <code>getDataT4()</code> function, returning what is needed to build the required accordion in the template.</li>
          <li>Finish the <code>block solution_accordion</code> in the file <code>templates/test/blocks_test.twig</code> using the returned value of the mentioned function to build the requested accordion, leaving the style to you.</li>
          <li>Showcase only 15 countries in the accordion.</li>
          <li>There are multiple solutions to this approach, use the one that is easier for you.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="task"><em>The optional requirements are:</em>
        <ul>
          <li>If the section have a website, show it by using the proper FontAwesome icon and open it in a new page just after the code.</li>
          <li>The list of countries and or sections could be sorted by name too.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hints alert alert-primary" role="alert">
        <div><strong>Some hints:</strong></div>
        <ul>
          <li>You can check the relevant classes to see the existing functions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="task"><strong>The next image can be used as a reference for the output with one panel opened (it does not include the extra tasks).</strong></div>
      <div class="task accordion" id="exampleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pane1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pane1">
              Show Image
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="pane1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#exampleAccordion">
            <img src="./assets/img/task_1.png" alt="task1 example" class="img-fluid"/>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="solution_container">
        {% block solution_accordion %}
          <div class="solution_header">The solution for task 4 will appear here after the block is finished.</div>
        {% endblock %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="separation">

    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 5 <span class="badge badge-advanced">Advanced</span></div>
      <div class="task">Using the same class file from the task before, we want to get some extra information from a dataset existing in a XLSX file, that already exists in the root folder of the project (codes.xlsx).</div>
      <div class="task">If you open the document, you will see a set of codes, and we want to know the status of each code. If the card exists, will return some data. On the other hand, if the card does not exist, there will be no data in the response.</div>
      <div class="task">We would like to have a nice output of the result, by reading the XLSX file (be careful about possible headers), checking each card againts the API through the proper function available, and display all the results using a table (we leave the styling up to you).</div>
      <div class="task"><strong>The main requirements are:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Complete the <code>getDataT5()</code> function, returning what is needed to build the required table.</li>
          <li>Finish the <code>block solution_table</code> in the file <code>templates/test/blocks_test.twig</code> using the returned value of the mentioned function to build the proposed table.</li>
          <li>Each row of the table needs to have, if the card exists, the code of the card, the section code and the status. If the card does not exist, then we need to show the card with a message next to it in the table.</li>
          <li>There are multiple solutions to this approach, use the one that is easier for you.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="task"><em>The optional requirements are:</em>
        <ul>
          <li>Sort the results by code.</li>
          <li>Include in the table the activation date and the expiration date as well, taking in consideration that each card is valid for a year counting from the moment it was activated.</li>
          <li>If the card contains a section code, we can add the section name as well next to it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hints alert alert-primary" role="alert">
        <div><strong>Some hints:</strong></div>
        <ul>
          <li>The PHPOffice library is already available in the vendor folder.</li>
          <li>The hints of task 4 are also applicable to task 5.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="solution_container">
        {% block solution_table %}
          <div class="solution_header">The solution for task 5 will appear here after the block is finished.</div>
        {% endblock %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="separation">

    <div class="tasks_group">
      <div class="task_header">Task 6 <span class="badge badge-easy">Easy</span></div>
      <div class="task">Congratulations, there are no more tasks.</div>
      <div class="task">If you are doing this test as part of an assignment, please send <code>src/Test</code>, <code>assets/css/test_style.css</code> and <code>templates/test</code> files and folders to the email given to you; do not commit the results as a PR.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
